    {
      "id": "claim_e123ef685ae84c15b993090df350d638",
      "statement": "The `Database` wrapper requires PostgreSQL `user` and `password`, connects immediately with defaults `127.0.0.1:5432/stocksdb2` unless overridden, and creates one cursor for the connection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/database.py#L4-L7",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:24b24a39abfc618d0c8e5e6d586bfc775d6543443fbc71d54d746c69e291652b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_228d4ce989aa430eb54e53d329136216",
      "statement": "`Database.execute_query` executes with parameters only when the supplied `params` value is truthy and commits after each successful execution; `fetch_all` returns the current cursor's `fetchall()` result, while `close` closes cursor then connection. The wrapper has no rollback or exception-handling path, so psycopg2 errors surface to callers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/database.py#L9-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:30fc458dcd557483f3726c110f5df78f637068f0d312a04ae650dd1a888649a2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f80319af9e1644f8add7ef9c3393ef4e",
      "statement": "The active `src/app.py` entrypoint starts `StockSimulator` from `src/login.py`, whose login handler only prints credentials; there are no repository callers of `Database`. The root-level prototype scripts instead use psycopg2 directly, so their persistence behavior is not behavior of the active application or the wrapper.",
